f'The 52 transformer arrow initializers execute **{arrow_initializations:,} times** and the arrows are invoked **{tot["transformerArrowCalls"]:,} times**. These are initializer executions, not a claim about allocations surviving V8 optimization. The arrows replace {arrow_initializations:,} cached method reads with {tot["transformerArrowCalls"]:,} per-call reads (net {net_transform:,}). The `factory` property bindings stay in place. All original 127 direct uses and 46 value references stay unchanged: 44 callback arguments plus two branches of one conditional callback argument. Every arrow uses the exact declared parameter list and return type, without rest parameters. All 52 arrow `context` identifiers resolve to their transformer’s own parameter.','',
f'The printer resolves ten members once per entry: {tot["printerAliases"]:,} member reads, matching the original ten-member destructure, plus one object alias per entry. The two defaults use `??`; the same handlers object and original function values are retained. No printer use is rewritten. The three existing sentinel comparisons remain. Their total execution count is {tot["printerAliasSentinelIdentity"]:,}; the broader registered-function observer counts only comparisons involving a registered function value, not all default-sentinel executions.','',
'## Four counter checks and attribution','',
'The final observer unwraps optional types and follows base interfaces, including TextChangesWriter extending PrintHandlers. Its late-registration counter checks that receivers are observed at creation, rather than inferring lifetime coverage from a zero write total. Earlier counting versions with entry-only gaps are not used to support the final lifetime-write claim.','', 'Counters run only in private counting copies. Writes cover all NodeFactory/PrintHandlers members and the taken method-signature members of TransformationContext; its unchanged factory property and mutable transformation hooks are outside that latter scope. Instrumentation installation writes are excluded. In-place data-property accessors preserve receiver objects and function values; typed assignment sites and Object.defineProperty calls are also observed. Function length getters retain the original length value. Equality observations retain the original comparison expression for TypeScript narrowing, and inspect only side-effect-free local/constant operands. The prototype has none of this instrumentation. A separate virtual-source negative control reports all five unsafe references/declarations (shorthand value use, both assignment references, a shadowed local and a shadowed receiver) with file:line, exits 2, and performs zero compiler-source writes.','',
f'- Writes: setter {tot["observedSetterWrites"]}, typed assignment {tot["typedAssignmentWrites"]}, defineProperty {tot["definePropertyWrites"]}. These instruments overlap and must not be summed as distinct writes. Observer descriptor failures: {len(counts["failures"])}. Late receiver registrations: `{json.dumps(late,sort_keys=True)}`; creation-time coverage is limited wherever a late registration is reported.','',
f'- Identity: direct receiver comparisons {tot["receiverIdentity"]}; broader registered-function comparisons {tot["memberIdentityComparisons"]:,}. Per-site counts are in [split-counts.json](evidence/split-counts.json). These include the preserved printer sentinel identity uses; a blanket zero claim for alias identity would be false. A shared implementation such as `noop` also participates in unrelated comparisons after it is registered.','',
